    <node id="FIONNUALA">
      <data key="k_name">FIONNUALA</data>
      <data key="k_type">PERSON</data>
      <data key="k_desc">"Fionnuala enjoys diving deep into game characters and looks forward to future discussions and analyses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala is a participant in the discussion, discussing the potential for connection and support in Dutch's later stages and its impact on his downfall."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala is a participant in the discussion, expressing interest in the game's power system and how it will balance with exploration and combat."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala is a participant in the discussion, providing insights on games like 'Mass Effect Legendary Edition', 'Final Fantasy XVI', and 'Hollow Knight', emphasizing the emotional impact of their soundtracks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala is a participant in the discussion, sharing her positive experience with the Control Center and engaging in conversations about game mechanics and recommendations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala is a player who shares a hilarious glitch where Arthur floats in mid-air during a cutscene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala is interested in a good matchmaking system and a solid tutorial or training mode to enhance the gameplay experience."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala is a participant in the discussion who discusses how emotional ties with NPCs make gaming experiences unforgettable and influence replay value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala is a participant in the discussion, describing an unexpected dragon fight in 'Skyrim' while on a quest, resulting in a chaotic and exciting experience."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala is a participant in the discussion, highlighting the immersive and surreal nature of the forested areas through sound and visuals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala is a participant in the discussion, suggesting ideas for game mechanics and character roles, particularly focusing on intelligence-based characters and gameplay diversity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala is a participant who praises "All Ghillied Up" and discusses the emotional impact of missions in Call of Duty games."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fionnuala is a participant who shares her experience with the 'What Lies Unseen' quest and the emotional impact of choices."</data>
      <data key="k_deg">6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GAVRIEL">
      <data key="k_name">GAVRIEL</data>
      <data key="k_type">PERSON</data>
      <data key="k_desc">"Gavriel enjoys discussions about characters and games, looking forward to future chats and exploring new content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is a participant in the discussion, analyzing the bond between Dutch and Arthur and the potential for support and change if Dutch had listened to Arthur."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is a participant in the discussion, discussing the erosion of trust within the gang due to Dutch van der Linde's reckless decisions and his transformation into a dictator."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is a participant in the discussion, looking forward to diverse enemy encounters and unique combat strategies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is a participant in the discussion, appreciating "Final Fantasy VII Remake" for its character development and plot twists."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is a participant in the discussion, emphasizing the emotional impact of Arthur's growth and the game's character development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is a participant in the discussion, sharing his preference for turn-based combat and engaging in conversations about game mechanics and recommendations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is a player who recounts a ridiculous glitch where their horse walks backwards during a mission."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is excited about crafting systems in games, as they offer opportunities for creating unique weapons and gear and encourage exploration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is a participant in the discussion who discusses the emotional impact of animal NPCs, particularly Trico from "The Last Guardian," and their unique role in games."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is a participant in the discussion, commenting on the visuals and atmosphere in 'Spider-Man: Miles Morales' and 'Resident Evil Village'."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is a participant in the discussion, expressing awe at the mountain regions and their realistic snow effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is a participant in the discussion, sharing his experience with big bosses in 'Bloodborne', particularly Artorias."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is a participant in the discussion, sharing their appreciation for 'Skyrim' and 'The Witcher 3', highlighting the game's quests and landscapes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is a participant in the discussion, suggesting 'Gris' as a game that appears simple but explores themes of grief and emotional growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is a participant in the discussion, suggesting gadgets that manipulate enemy communications and devices that disable enemy weapons, as well as diverse settings for missions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is a participant who discusses the lack of clear-cut answers in the game and the emotional weight of decisions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gavriel is a participant who suggests bringing back characters like Price or Soap for nostalgia and emotional connections."</data>
      <data key="k_deg">12</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CAELUM">
      <data key="k_name">CAELUM</data>
      <data key="k_type">PERSON</data>
      <data key="k_desc">"Caelum has had fun experiences with crossplay and is hoping the new game will support it, allowing for coordinated strategies with friends on different platforms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caelum is a participant in the discussion, emphasizing the emotional investment and storytelling in games."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caelum is a participant in the discussion, emphasizing the significance of character development and the contrast between growth and stagnation in storytelling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caelum is a participant in the discussion, focusing on the challenge of using powers effectively in combat and adapting strategies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caelum is excited about future discussions on games and characters, looking forward to continuing the conversation with others."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caelum is a participant in the discussion, focusing on the game's stunning landscapes and the immersive experience of exploring locations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caelum is a participant in the discussion, reflecting on how the story of "Red Dead Redemption 2" influenced his gameplay choices and emotional engagement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caelum is a participant in the discussion, sharing his preference for turn-based combat and engaging in conversations about game mechanics and recommendations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caelum is a participant in the discussion who reflects on the bond with the horse in "Red Dead Redemption 2" and how it becomes a significant part of the player's story."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caelum is a participant in the discussion, expressing admiration for the visuals in 'Final Fantasy VII Remake' and 'Horizon Forbidden West'."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caelum is a participant in the discussion, recommending 'Oxenfree' for its natural dialogue system and deep character dynamics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caelum is a participant in the discussion, recounting an unexpected monster battle in 'The Witcher 3' that was both challenging and thrilling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caelum is a participant in the discussion, suggesting locations like Tokyo and Machu Picchu for urban and historical warfare, incorporating local mythology and history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Caelum is a participant who appreciates the depth of storytelling in Witcher 3 and the lasting impact of choices on characters."</data>
